# Build outputs. Every path below is written by `npm run build` and none of it
# belongs in a commit.
#
# `js/auth-worker.js` is wrangler's `main`. While it was tracked, a plain
# `wrangler deploy` uploaded whatever bundle happened to be committed and
# exited 0 — so a source change that nobody rebuilt would not reach production
# and the deploy would still succeed. Untracked, the same deploy fails with
# "The entry-point file at js/auth-worker.js was not found", and `npm run
# deploy` builds first. ADR-2608138000; the fleet-wide survey is ADR-2608136200.
#
# `js/` is not obviously a build directory by name, which is precisely how this
# one stayed invisible: a path-shaped audit looking for dist/ or build/ missed
# it entirely.
js/
# shadow-cljs :browser output-dir and the render-pages target. The Worker
# inlines both with shadow.resource/inline, so they are compile inputs to
# js/auth-worker.js and generated by the same `npm run build`.
resources/itonami/auth/app.js
resources/itonami/auth/manifest.edn
resources/itonami/auth/sign-in.html
